\vspace{-2mm}\paragraph{\bf Nooses and combinatorial nooses.} A \emph{noose} of a $\Sigma$-{plane} graph $G$ is
 a simple closed curve in $\Sigma$ that meets $G$ only in vertices.
  From the Jordan Curve Theorem, it then follows that nooses
separate $\Sigma$ into two regions. %  $\Delta_1$ and $\Delta_2$.
