\cup N_e$, where  $G_i$ is the
graph induced by the edge~set~$\{\mu(f): f \in L \cap V(T_i) \}$ for $i \in \{1,2\}$ and $T_1 \dot{\cup} T_2 = T\setminus \{e\}$. Thus $N_e$ meets $G$ only in
$V(N_e)=\mids(e)$ and its length is $|\mids(e)|$. %A clockwise traversal
%of $N_e$ in the drawing of $G$ defines a cyclic ordering $\pi$
%of $\mids(e)$.
  The vertices of every middle
set~$\mids(e) = V(G_1) \cap V(G_2)$ are enumerated according to a 
 cyclic permutation $\pi$ on $\mids(e)$.
